  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"122\" data-end=\"325\">Factor II, or <strong data-start=\"136\" data-end=\"151\">prothrombin</strong>, is a <strong data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"197\">vitamin K&ndash;dependent clotting factor</strong> synthesized in the liver. It is converted to thrombin in the coagulation cascade, playing a <strong data-start=\"290\" data-end=\"324\">central role in clot formation</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"327\" data-end=\"459\">The <strong data-start=\"331\" data-end=\"351\">functional assay</strong> measures the activity level of Factor II in plasma, often expressed as a <strong data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"439\">percentage</strong> of normal activity.</p>\n<p data-start=\"953\" data-end=\"990\"><strong data-start=\"958\" data-end=\"990\">Decreased Factor II Activity</strong></p>\n<p data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1039\">Indicates <strong data-start=\"1001\" data-end=\"1024\">hypoprothrombinemia</strong>, which may be:</p>\n<ol data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1505\">\n<li data-start=\"1040\" data-end=\"1152\">\n<p data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1065\"><strong data-start=\"1043\" data-end=\"1064\">Congenital (rare)</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1069\" data-end=\"1152\">\n<li data-start=\"1069\" data-end=\"1090\">\n<p data-start=\"1071\" data-end=\"1090\">Autosomal recessive</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1094\" data-end=\"1152\">\n<p data-start=\"1096\" data-end=\"1152\">Presents with mild to severe bleeding depending on level</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1154\" data-end=\"1505\">\n<p data-start=\"1157\" data-end=\"1184\"><strong data-start=\"1157\" data-end=\"1183\">Acquired (more common)</strong>:</p>\n<ul data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1505\">\n<li data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1271\">\n<p data-start=\"1190\" data-end=\"1271\"><strong data-start=\"1190\" data-end=\"1214\">Vitamin K deficiency</strong> (e.g., malnutrition, malabsorption, biliary obstruction)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1275\" data-end=\"1338\">\n<p data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1338\"><strong data-start=\"1277\" data-end=\"1294\">Liver disease</strong> (since prothrombin is synthesized in liver)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1342\" data-end=\"1391\">\n<p data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1391\"><strong data-start=\"1344\" data-end=\"1374\">Oral anticoagulant therapy</strong> (e.g., warfarin)</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1395\" data-end=\"1445\">\n<p data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1445\"><strong data-start=\"1397\" data-end=\"1445\">Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1449\" data-end=\"1505\">\n<p data-start=\"1451\" data-end=\"1505\"><strong data-start=\"1451\" data-end=\"1505\">Presence of inhibitors (e.g., lupus anticoagulant)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p data-start=\"1507\" data-end=\"1534\"><strong data-start=\"1512\" data-end=\"1534\">Increased Activity</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1711\">\n<li data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1578\">\n<p data-start=\"1537\" data-end=\"1578\">Rarely clinically significant on its own.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1579\" data-end=\"1711\">\n<p data-start=\"1581\" data-end=\"1711\">May be seen in inflammatory states or <strong data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1656\">Factor II gene mutation (G20210A)</strong>, which is associated with a <strong data-start=\"1685\" data-end=\"1710\">hypercoagulable state</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
